WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.835
-Welcome back, everybody!

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.369
We're here with Oscar Isaac!

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:04.470
Come on, now.

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.638
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:08.641
We love you.
His movie "The Card Counter"

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:10.409
is On Demand now.

00:00:10.409 --> 00:00:12.311
"The Card Counter,"
you play a guy

00:00:12.311 --> 00:00:14.213
who has actually mastered how
to count cards

00:00:14.213 --> 00:00:16.182
and goes casino to casino,

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.550
winning little amounts
of money...

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.618
-Little bit
-...just enough

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:20.152
to make a living.

00:00:20.152 --> 00:00:22.522
Paul Schrader, director.
-Yeah, the great Paul Schrader.

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:24.190
-I mean, dude, "Taxi Driver,"
"Raging Bull."

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.693
Come on, he's legendary.
Produced by Scorsese?

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:29.329
-Mm-hmm.
-Yeah, not too shabby.

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:31.064
Do you know how to play cards,
at all, or just acting?

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:32.631
-A little bit, a little,
you know, poker.

00:00:32.631 --> 00:00:34.000
-You do?
-Yeah, a little bit of poker.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.136
-Oh, wow. Did you gamble
during the movie?

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:38.338
-So we shot in an actual casino,

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:40.139
actual casinos
in Biloxi, Mississippi...

00:00:40.139 --> 00:00:41.473
-Yeah.
-...and, in between takes,

00:00:41.473 --> 00:00:43.509
I'd go and sit with the locals
and play a little bit.

00:00:43.509 --> 00:00:44.543
-Oh, really?
-Yeah.

00:00:44.543 --> 00:00:45.912
-And are you...good?

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:47.547
-Bet low, lose low, you know?
-Yeah.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:48.981
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.981 --> 00:00:50.916
Tiffany Haddish is in this,
who we love.

00:00:50.916 --> 00:00:53.920
Who is so funny, but in this
movie, dramatic role.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.622
-Yeah, it's a role that,
you know,

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:56.689
she doesn't really get
to play often

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:58.091
and she's just so great in it.

00:00:58.091 --> 00:00:59.592
-Isn't something?
I go,

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:01.260
I've never met anyone
like Tiffany Haddish.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:04.096
-I mean, I said to her,
I was like --

00:01:04.096 --> 00:01:05.498
Well, the first thing she said,
when I was like,

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:06.565
"Hi, Tiffany.
How are you doing?"

00:01:06.565 --> 00:01:07.634
She's like, "Successful."

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:10.002
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.002 --> 00:01:12.939
-That's a good answer.
Yeah, yeah, a little successful.

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:14.473
-Immediately, I was like,
"I love this person."

00:01:14.473 --> 00:01:17.142
[ Laughter ]
And she just exudes
such a vibrancy.

00:01:17.142 --> 00:01:18.878
It's like I imagine it was like

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.346
what meeting Jesus was like.

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:21.680
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, wow.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.216
-Where you're just like,
"I'll follow you.

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:24.617
I'll follow you anywhere."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:27.319
You know, I just want to be
around that light, you know?

00:01:27.319 --> 00:01:29.088
-She does have a good --
-Like a sexy Jesus.

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:30.923
-Yeah, of course, yeah, exactly.
-Like really sexy Jesus.

00:01:30.923 --> 00:01:33.126
-Do you want to set up what
"The Card Counter" is about?

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:34.894
-Well, yeah. Like you said,
it's about this man

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:39.298
who went to prison
and learned how to count cards

00:01:39.298 --> 00:01:41.100
and, when he gets out,

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.970
he feels that he still
deserves punishment

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.571
for the horrible things
that he did.

00:01:45.571 --> 00:01:46.672
It's a dark movie.

00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:47.740
It's Paul Schrader,
again, you know.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.510
This isn't like a flashy,
fun casino movie.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:53.045
It's heavy stuff,
but really moving, I think.

00:01:53.045 --> 00:01:56.215
And, any way,
he's given himself over

00:01:56.215 --> 00:01:57.983
to this like
purgatorial existence

00:01:57.983 --> 00:02:00.920
where he just goes and,
you know, plays these cards

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.289
and just kind of is going to
run out the clock on his life

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:04.957
and then,
he meets these two people

00:02:04.957 --> 00:02:07.727
that give him a window
into possible redemption.

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:08.794
-Yeah.
It's really good.

00:02:08.794 --> 00:02:09.929
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:11.698
Here's Oscar Isaac
in "The Card Counter."

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:12.832
Take a look.

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:15.068
-Am I trying to justify
what we did?

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:19.038
[ Suspenseful music plays ]

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:20.106
No.

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:24.611
♪♪

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:25.745
[ Crying ]
Nothing...

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:28.047
♪♪

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:30.349
...nothing can justify
what we did.

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:34.520
♪♪

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.088
Your father understood that.

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:38.557
♪♪

00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:40.259
If you were there,
you could understand.

00:02:40.259 --> 00:02:42.060
♪♪

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:45.131
Otherwise, there's no

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:47.299
understanding.

00:02:47.299 --> 00:02:48.968
-Yeah.
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.370
Oscar Isaac, everybody.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.838
"The Card Counter" is
On Demand now.

00:02:52.838 --> 00:02:54.206
Congrats on everything, buddy.
-Thank you, brother.

00:02:54.206 --> 00:02:57.110
-Couldn't happen to a nicer guy.
Oscar Isaac, everybody.

